Portable compiler using interpreter metaprogramming with ARM64 and x86-64
native object backends. Translated with src/bootstrap/wasm2c.c when a native
seed is unavailable or cannot compile the current sources.

proof (scripts/compiler/refresh-seed.sh wasm):
- wasm-tools validation with memory64 enabled, when wasm-tools is installed.
- every env import is defined by src/bootstrap/runtime.c with its exact type.
- translated with wasm2c and linked against runtime.c on macOS ARM64.
- the translated compiler checks main.coil and main_a64.coil, and builds a
  native main_a64.coil stage1 that runs src/examples/fib.coil (exit 55).

The Linux x86-64 native seeds are not refreshed on this host. Their automatic
fallback is this portable seed (then the Linux bootstrap IR); actual Linux
x86-64 self-host verification remains the Linux CI job's responsibility.
